MassCubeX
Copyright 2026 MassCubeX contributors

Derived from huaxuyu/masscube, commit
356748ede691862b9a87f67812db5e728a703b9d (MassCube 1.2.22 by Huaxu Yu).
MassCubeX provides streaming mzML/mzXML input, adaptive MS1 noise estimation,
MS/MS provenance and per-file Parquet/TSV output. Core scientific algorithms
follow upstream; original function bodies for feature finalization, segmentation,
scores and centroid merging are retained in src/masscubex/upstream.py.
An optimized trace tracker preserves upstream matching and ordering rules.
Automatic calibration, profile MS1 mass detection and MS2-seeded raw-MS1 gap
filling are configurable extensions enabled by default. Greedy grouping derives from upstream
feature_grouping.py and uses the selected configurable ion catalog.
Packaging and documentation have been rewritten. Vendor readers, alignment,
library annotation, statistics and plotting are outside the extraction command.
The original Apache License 2.0 and attribution above are retained.
Unmodified reference functions are also retained in tests/upstream_masscube.py.

SciPy compatibility algorithms
The Gaussian reflection, plateau detection, distance selection and prominence
routines in src/masscubex/chromatograms.py follow the semantics and accumulation
order of SciPy 1.13.1 (scipy/ndimage/src/ni_filters.c and
scipy/signal/_peak_finding_utils.pyx), adapted to readable Numba kernels.
